{title: 370 - Christ for the World}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #370 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 370}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Christ for the [Gm]world [C]we [F]sing, [F]The [C]world [F]to [C7]Christ [F]we [C]bring,
[F]With loving [C]zeal;
[C]The poor, [C7]and [F]them that mourn, [C]The faint [C7]and [F]overborne,
[F]Sin-sick and sorrow-worn, [Gm]Whom [C]Christ [C7]doth [F]heal.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F][Gm]Christ [C][F]for [F]the [C][F]world [C7][F]we [C]sing,
[F]the world to [C]Christ we bring,
[C][C7]with [F][C]fervent [C7][F]prayer;
[F]the [Gm]wayward [C]and [C7]the [F]lost,
[F][Gm][C]by [F][F]restless [C][F][C7]passions [F][C]tossed,
[F]redeemed at [C]countless cost,
[C][C7]from [F][C]dark [C7][F]despair.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F][Gm]Christ [C][F]for [F]the [C][F]world [C7][F]we [C]sing,
[F]the world to [C]Christ we bring,
[C][C7]with [F][C]joyful [C7][F]song;
[F]the [Gm]newborn [C]souls, [C7]whose [F]days,
[F][Gm][C]reclaimed [F][F]from [C][F][C7]error's [F][C]ways,
[F]inspired with [C]hope and praise,
[C][C7]to [F][C]Christ [C7][F]belong.
{end_of_verse}
